Date: Fri, 09 Oct 2026 16:51:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 25/25] WebAPI: Keep field hashes instead of torrent copies for
 sync/maindata

To send only what changed, every sync/maindata session kept a copy of every
torrent's fields as a QVariantMap (about 10 KiB per torrent with all its
strings and map nodes): 90 MB per WebUI session with ~9,000 torrents, held
until the session expires. A full update the client had not confirmed yet
held another reference to it.

A session now keeps, per torrent, a 64-bit hash of each field's JSON text
(the key list is shared by all torrents with the same fields): about 0.5 KiB
per torrent. A field is sent when its hash differs, or, if it is missing
from the previous digest, when it is not null, as before. Full updates are
written straight from the torrents; until the client confirms one, the
session only notes that all torrents have to be sent again.
